# Phase 5: Project Testing Phase

## Project Title: EduGenie – Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant

### 1. Introduction

The Project Testing Phase is an important stage in the development of EduGenie. It focuses on checking the functionality, performance, usability, and reliability of the application.

The main purpose of testing is to identify errors, verify that all features work correctly, and ensure that students can use the AI-powered learning assistant smoothly.

### 2. Objectives of Testing

1. Verify that the AI chatbot generates responses correctly.

2. Check the integration of Google Gemini API.

3. Test the notes generation feature.

4. Verify the text summarization functionality.

5. Check the exam preparation module.

6. Identify and fix software errors.

7. Ensure a user-friendly experience.

### 3. Types of Testing

1. Functional Testing

Checks whether all application features work according to the requirements.

2. Integration Testing

Verifies the communication between the frontend, Flask backend, and Google Gemini API.

3. Usability Testing

Checks whether students can easily navigate and use the application.

4. Performance Testing

Evaluates response time and application behavior under normal usage.

5. Error Handling Testing

Checks how the system handles empty inputs, invalid requests, API errors, and internet connectivity issues.

